REMEDIATIONS  (DNS-side fixes first: they hold regardless of routing)
  domain-owner      publish CAA with issue=<your CA>; accounturi=<ACME account>
                    closes: mis-issuance by every other CA and account
  dns-host          sign the zone and publish the DS at the registrar
                    closes: forged 'no CAA' answers after a nameserver hijack
  registrar         enable DNSSEC for the domain (DS publication)
                    closes: the same, from the registrar side
  dns-host          set ROA maxLength equal to the announced prefix length (RFC 9319) for nameserver prefixes
                    closes: RPKI-valid more-specific hijacks of the nameservers
  hosting-provider  set ROA maxLength equal to the announced prefix length (RFC 9319) for web prefixes
                    closes: RPKI-valid more-specific hijacks of the web servers

